# AudioSuite-Pro .mailmap — one canonical identity for the whole history.
# Changed in 2.7.0: added as the pre-sale diligence record that reconciles the
# two author identities below; see TECHNICAL_CHANGELOG.md.
#
# Added 2026-11-11 as part of the pre-sale diligence pack. The history contains
# two identities for the same author: the GitHub noreply address used from one
# machine (`33846991+wilte01@users.noreply.github.com`, 313 commits) and the
# account email (`wilte01@gmail.com`, 181 commits). Left alone, a two-name git
# log reads to a buyer's counsel as two copyright owners, and the IP warranty
# becomes a question instead of a statement.
#
# This file reconciles the two for every git command that honours mailmap
# (git shortlog, git log --use-mailmap, git blame --use-mailmap, git
# format-patch). It does not rewrite history, deliberately: rewriting would
# invalidate every commit hash cited by the PLAN_*.md and AUDIT_*.md records
# that document why each change was made.
#
# Canonical identity — confirmed by the repository owner:
#   Terrence Williams <wilte01@gmail.com>
#
Terrence Williams <wilte01@gmail.com> <33846991+wilte01@users.noreply.github.com>
